      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Starting your garment washing service with SDF Clothing follows a structured process designed to ensure your wash requirements are understood and results meet expectations. The process begins with providing detailed specifications, after which we guide you through sample development and bulk processing.</p>
        
        <p>Step one is to submit your washing requirements through our contact form or email. Essential information includes: garment type and fabric composition, wash type preference (enzyme, stone, bleach, acid, silicon, pigment), desired effect description, target quantity per style and color, and desired timeline. If you have reference samples showing desired wash effects, include them for clarity. For garments we manufacture, washing specifications are coordinated with our production team.</p>
        
        <p>Step two involves our technical review and quotation. Within 24-48 hours of receiving your requirements, we provide a detailed quotation including washing costs, processing time, quality assurance, and any additional services. The quotation specifies lead times for sampling and bulk processing, minimum order quantities, and payment terms. For complex or custom wash requirements, we may request sample garments for parameter development. You may request revisions to the quotation to adjust specifications to meet budget targets.</p>
        
        <p>Step three is sample washing and approval. After quotation acceptance, we proceed with sample development, typically taking 5-7 days for standard washes and 7-10 days for complex treatments. Samples are shipped to you for review, and we provide detailed inspection reports documenting wash results. You may approve samples as-is, request parameter adjustments, or proceed with additional sample rounds. Each sample round adds 3-5 days but ensures the final wash effect meets your expectations. We recommend thorough sample approval before bulk processing.</p>
        
        <p>Step four is bulk washing confirmation. Once wash parameters are approved, we require a deposit to confirm processing and schedule production. Standard terms are 30% deposit with order confirmation and 70% before shipment. Processing begins after deposit receipt and garment receipt. We provide a processing schedule with key milestones including washing completion, drying and finishing, and expected delivery date. Throughout processing, we provide status updates on batch progress.</p>
        
        <p>Step five is final inspection and delivery. Before shipment, we conduct final quality inspection using our standard protocols with additional verification that wash effects meet specifications. We provide an inspection report for your review. Once inspection is approved, we finalize packaging and prepare shipping documentation. Balance payment is required before release of washed garments. We provide all necessary documentation for your records and any regulatory requirements.</p>
        
        <p>Throughout the process, our team provides technical guidance on wash selection, parameter optimization, and effect achievement. We understand that washing is both an art and a science, requiring expertise to achieve consistent results. Clear communication about your desired effects and quality expectations helps us deliver washed garments that meet your specifications and enhance your product offerings.</p>
